{"ts": 1792666251.248426, "iso": "2026-10-22T10:50:51", "event": "meta_wipe_recovery", "payload": {"note": "Poll run 2026-10-22T10:50Z. No canon_changed event written and none is claimable: the canon endpoint live-canon.superinstance.dev/api/canon returned HTTP 503 Service Unavailable from Cloudflare's edge (TLS_error SAN verify failure reaching origin, identical with and without cert verification), so poll_canon() took its exception path and returned canon_hash=None. Critically, there is still no state.json in this directory, so load_state() yields last_hash=None and the script has NEVER recorded a successful baseline hash in its entire witness history; every one of the 9 prior entries is bot_started/poll_failed (503 on 09-21, 403 on 09-21 and 10-02). This changes over 20 days with zero observed canon transitions, and the 403s on 09-21/10-02 were most likely an auth-mode regression rather than an outage. A watcher that has never established a baseline cannot detect a change -- the 'no change' branch is unreachable until one successful poll lands, which is the same fail-silent shape as the monitor-with-no-emitter defect found in spreadsheet-engine. Environment note: /workspace is again 100% full (600G/600G, 0 bytes avail on the NAS mount), so even a 1-byte write fails; the script's 4 hardcoded /workspace/... paths were repointed to /tmp/wm-run/bots/ to execute, matching the 10-02 recovery. A git clone of AI-Writings into /workspace fails outright on quota (Disk quota exceeded) and the clone into /tmp hung with --filter=blob:none, so recovery was done via contents API + raw.githubusercontent. No witness note about canon change is written because no canon data was retrieved; a 503 is not a state transition.", "recovered_via": "GitHub contents API + raw.githubusercontent (clone blocked by NAS quota)", "git_sha": "9125e7dc81f2ea0e001871e54c10700855134067", "canon_poll": "FAILED 503 \u2014 no baseline hash ever recorded; no state.json in repo", "workspace_status": "NAS mount 100% full, 0 bytes available"}, "hash": "RECOVERED"}
