 mismatch was BORN WITH THE ROW in upstream commit 43b98389 and propagated unchanged through 092a4e64, d709e263, 76b840e, b88a6d2e and 6cdb2ccf; it is not a post-hoc payload edit and is not caused by this run. Honest verdict: 36/36 rows accounted for, of which 33 verify, 2 are RECOVERED markers, 1 is a stale hash from an upstream authoring slip; NOT 'chain-intact'. This run's own row 36 self-verifies (94a26bf614e22a7f). Environment (13th consecutive wipe with the named path gone): /workspace/repos/ai-writings/... did not exist again; /workspace was an empty NAS mount at 600G/600G, 100%, 0 bytes available. Recovery this run: a full clone of SuperInstance/AI-Writings to the overlay filesystem at /opt/work (28G free) rather than the NAS -- the NAS clone died on 'Disk quota exceeded' -- then staged the required files to /tmp/wm-run/bots/ because the script hardcodes those paths for witness.log/state.json/bookkeeper.wal and does sys.path.insert('/tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus') -- substrate_bus must be staged alongside it or the import dies. Staged script md5 206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267, byte-identical to the upstream git blob and to the value recorded in every prior run; no code changes were needed this run. SUBSTRATE TRUNCATION TRAP, re-verified live this run rather than assumed: the NAS accepts writes and silently truncates them to 0 bytes while reporting success, so a file can appear present in ls -la while holding nothing. substrate_bus.py hardcodes its write target to /workspace/repos/ai-writings/bots/substrate-bus/, so the substrate witness would have been lost. Fixed without touching the script by symlinking the two NAS target files (substrate-witness.jsonl, topics.json) to their /tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus/ counterparts; a probe write through the symlink HELD bytes (440 -> 471), after which the substrate log was restored byte-exactly to its upstream 440-byte state (md5 e1240259a3f082af0aacde5c117bbf96) so no probe row contaminates the record. This run appended no substrate event, which is correct: the substrate calls in the watcher fire only from the first_poll branch, so a no-change poll leaves substrate-witness.jsonl byte-unchanged. CARRIED FORWARD, still PROVEN rather than merely reported: the bookkeeper budget=1000.0 vs gamma+eta=70.0 defect. The predicate abs(gamma+eta-budget) < 1e-6 or (delta_gamma==0 and delta_eta==0) has an UNREACHABLE (0,0) escape clause on every call path (first_poll always passes delta_gamma=1.0; canon_changed always passes delta_eta=1.0), and the first clause can only pass if the running total hits EXACTLY 1000.0 within 1e-6, which is a coincidence target rather than a conservation law. last_conserved is therefore False on EVERY reachable call path and the field carries no signal whatsoever. Seventh poll reporting this; still unfixed. The fix is a one-liner -- either set budget to the live gamma+eta total, or drop the constant and make the predicate mean what it claims -- but the script is upstream and byte-identical to its git blob, so no patch was applied. Also observed this run: the upstream witness.log ends with a bot_started row at 2026-10-23T16:46:32Z (pid 218) that was never followed by a witness_note, i.e. the previous poll was launched but its note was not written. This run starts from that orphaned bot_started row, which is why the pre-run row count was 35 rather than 34."}, "hash": "ad118540bbd29608"}
