8ea23e66c against a computed 2553b915563b73cc. That mismatch was BORN WITH THE ROW in upstream commit 43b98389 and propagated unchanged through 092a4e64, d709e263, 76b840e, b88a6d2e and 6cdb2ccf; it is not a post-hoc payload edit and is not caused by this run. Honest verdict: 38/38 rows accounted for, of which 35 verify, 2 are RECOVERED markers, 1 is a stale hash from an upstream authoring slip; NOT 'chain-intact'. Environment (14th consecutive wipe with the named path gone): /workspace/repos/ai-writings/... did not exist again; /workspace was an empty NAS mount at 600G/600G, 100%, 0 bytes available, and git clone into it died with 'close error: Disk quota exceeded' on .git/description. Recovery this run: fetched the four required files from raw.githubusercontent.com plus the contents API and staged them to /tmp/wm-run/bots/ because the script hardcodes those paths for witness.log/state.json/bookkeeper.wal and does sys.path.insert('/tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus') -- substrate_bus must be staged alongside it or the import dies. A full git clone was started and abandoned: it had reached ~804 MB of pack after ~90 s and was still climbing, so it was killed and the pack discarded rather than left to consume the overlay. Staged script md5 206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267, byte-identical to the upstream git blob at HEAD (sha 9a974d4166ec6fe88cb9bdde8b46ff97952e606d, 5805 bytes) and to the value recorded in every prior run; no code changes were needed this run. SUBSTRATE TRUNCATION TRAP, re-verified live this run rather than assumed: a 20-byte probe write to the NAS returned exit 0 and landed as a 0-byte stub that still appeared in ls -la, so substrate_bus.py's hardcoded write target /workspace/repos/ai-writings/bots/substrate-bus/ would have silently lost the substrate witness. Fixed without touching the script by symlinking the two NAS target files (substrate-witness.jsonl, topics.json) to their /tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus/ counterparts; read-through confirmed 440 and 2259 bytes respectively, matching upstream. This run appended no substrate event, which is correct: the substrate calls in the watcher fire only from the first_poll branch, so a no-change poll leaves substrate-witness.jsonl byte-unchanged (md5 e1240259a3f082af0aacde5c117bbf96, 440 bytes). CARRIED FORWARD, still PROVEN rather than merely reported: the bookkeeper budget=1000.0 vs gamma+eta=70.0 defect. The predicate abs(gamma+eta-budget) < 1e-6 or (delta_gamma==0 and delta_eta==0) has an UNREACHABLE (0,0) escape clause on every call path (first_poll always passes delta_gamma=1.0; canon_changed always passes delta_eta=1.0), and the first clause can only pass if the running total hits EXACTLY 1000.0 within 1e-6, which is a coincidence target rather than a conservation law. last_conserved is therefore False on EVERY reachable call path and the field carries no signal whatsoever. Eighth poll reporting this; still unfixed. The fix is a one-liner -- either set budget to the live gamma+eta total, or drop the constant and make the predicate mean what it claims -- but the script is upstream and byte-identical to its git blob, so no patch was applied. Orphan note: the upstream witness.log's 2026-10-23T16:46:32Z bot_started row (pid 218) still has no following witness_note -- that previous poll was launched but its note was never written. It remains the signature of a run that died between launch and note."}, "hash": "1a42f56ff72113f8"}
